  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2009-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Starting inside, \\(1 + 1 = 2,\\) so \\(1 + \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{3}{2}.\\) Then \\(\\dfrac{1}{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\dfrac{2}{3},\\) and \\(1 + \\dfrac{2}{3} = \\dfrac{5}{3}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Work outward from the innermost fraction",
        "First simplify \\(1 + \\dfrac{1}{1+1} = \\dfrac{3}{2},\\) then take its reciprocal"
      ],
